# ── Customer-specific configuration (never commit) ───────────────────────
# The pipeline is domain-neutral: it reads *what* to process from rules/, and a
# customer deployment fills these with its own database schema, column codes,
# master code values and SME business rules. Those are the customer's asset —
# once pushed they stay in git history even if the file is deleted later.
#
# The files below exist only in a customer deployment; the repo ships no
# neutral counterpart, so they are ignored outright.
# 패턴은 ``rules/**/`` 로 쓴다. rules/ 는 domain/ policy/ contracts/ 하위 폴더로
# 나뉘어 있어 평평한 ``rules/<name>.json`` 패턴은 하위 폴더의 파일을 무시하지 못한다.
# 패턴을 추가하면 ``git check-ignore -v rules/domain/<name>.json`` 으로 적용을 확인한다.
rules/**/ddl_schema.json
rules/**/dimension_config.json
rules/**/column_dictionary.json
rules/**/code_meanings.json
rules/**/canonical_hints.json
rules/**/std_item_metadata.json
rules/**/sme_business_rules.json
rules/**/korean_synonyms.json
rules/**/user_term_dictionary.json
rules/**/*.bak_*
rules/**/*.suggested.json

# The remaining rules/*.json ARE tracked, holding domain-neutral defaults
# (example.com namespace, sample tables) that the server needs to boot at all —
# domain/namespaces.py raises without rules/domain/domain_config.json. A deployment
# overwrites them locally; run
#     git update-index --skip-worktree rules/<category>/<file>
# so those local edits can never be staged. Ignore rules and skip-worktree cover
# only the files named here, so review ``git diff --cached`` for customer values
# before each commit.

# Customer inputs and staged artifacts.
#
# Customer-authored domain docs live under docs/examples/ alongside the tracked
# neutral samples, so they are ignored by a naming convention rather than by
# customer name: prefix such files ``customer-`` (``docs/examples/customer-erd.md``).
# Naming the customer here would put its identity in a tracked file — the exact
# thing this repo's neutrality guarantee rules out.
data/source/query_tests/golden_sql/
data/source/master/
docs/sme/
docs/examples/customer-*

# Local-only Kiro CLI workspace (개인 컨텍스트, git 추적 제외)
.kiro/

# Session handoff (민감 정보 포함 — 딜/계정/이메일, git 추적 제외)
HANDOFF.md
